    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Failing Closed with Spring Boot',
         body=None,
         narration='Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains failing Closed with Spring, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] In a Spring Boot bank the decision must start as no, every call to another service needs a time budget, a limited retry and a breaker, a transfer is a unit of work only if the proxy and the rollback rules say so, and one error handler must give the customer a reference while the log keeps the reason; the safety costs availability, which is paid for with breakers and alerts. [[slnc 600]] Think of it this way. [[slnc 300]] A bank vault with an electronic lock. When the power fails, the door can lock itself or open itself. A vault that opens in a power cut is opened by cutting the power. Failing closed is the vault that locks, and the price is that nobody gets in until the power is back, which is why the bank also has a generator and an alarm. [[slnc 700]] In this video, the domain is an online bank. [[slnc 500]] By the end, you will be able to: [[slnc 300]] Explain why a decision must start as no. [[slnc 300]] Give every call to another service a budget, a limited retry and a breaker. [[slnc 300]] Name the two rules that make @Transactional leave a transfer half done.'),
